        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-09-11T21:06:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I didn\u0027t realize that the rest of the code was treating VBUS discharge as something that can be turned on and off. I thought it was expected to be a set-and-forget mechanic and that I had to take other measures (like this).\n\nVBUS drops down to 0 and then comes back up on connect, although I think it\u0027s from not adjusting my register write based on enable in syv682x_discharge_vbus. This code disables VBUS discharge, which I don\u0027t think should have an effect here. I can\u0027t confirm that it caused issues, but I did see a hard reset that I didn\u0027t attempt to attribute.\n\nIn any case, I think the other VBUS operations can assume that discharge was set appropriately, and I\u0027ll remove the discharge changes here.",
      "parentUuid": "121abc38_b74c13f4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 300,
        "startChar": 1,
